.\" phpall(1) — comprehensive all-in-one man page for phplang.
.\" Modeled after zshall(1): every section of the reference in one document.
.\" Render with:  man -l man/phpall.1
.\" Install:      cp man/phpall.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
.TH PHPALL 1 "2026-07-23" "phplang 0.2.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phpall \- the phplang comprehensive reference (invocation, language, architecture,
bytecode VM + Cranelift JIT, LSP, DAP, inline-Rust FFI)
.SH OVERVIEW
This is the all\-in\-one
.B phplang
manual, modeled on
.BR zshall (1).
It concatenates the major sections of the phplang reference into a single page so
you can grep with `/`:
.RS 2
.PP
.B 1.  INVOCATION
.RB "\(em " "flags, files, exit status"
.br
.B 2.  LANGUAGE
.RB "\(em " "the PHP the runtime parses and runs"
.br
.B 3.  ARCHITECTURE
.RB "\(em " "lex \[->] parse \[->] lower \[->] fusevm VM + JIT"
.br
.B 4.  TOOLING
.RB "\(em " "\-\-lsp, \-\-dap, inline-Rust FFI, dumps"
.br
.B 5.  DIAGNOSTICS
.RB "\(em " "error format and common messages"
.RE
.SH 1. INVOCATION
.B php
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR [\fIARGV\fR...] runs a PHP script.
.B \-r \fICODE\fR
runs code given on the command line, and
.B \-a
starts the interactive shell, and
.B \-d \fINAME\fR[=\fIVALUE\fR]
sets an ini entry before the source is read.
.B \-\-lsp
and
.B \-\-dap
speak their protocols over stdio and take no file. See
.BR php (1)
for the per\-flag table.
.SH 2. LANGUAGE
phplang runs PHP as ordinary compiled bytecode. Source files use the standard
\(oq\fI<?php ... ?>\fR\(cq and \(oq\fI<?= ... ?>\fR\(cq tags; any text outside a PHP
tag is passed through verbatim as inline HTML. It lexes and parses the source,
lowers it to
.B fusevm
instructions, and lets the shared engine execute and JIT\-compile them. Arithmetic
lowers to native fusevm ops; PHP object semantics \(em arrays, strings, and type
coercion \(em are served by the
.B PhpHost
runtime on top of the VM. It is the first compiled standalone PHP runtime.
.SH 3. ARCHITECTURE
.EX
PHP source \[->] lexer \[->] parser (AST) \[->] lower to fusevm bytecode \[->] fusevm VM + Cranelift JIT
.EE
.PP
There is no bespoke PHP VM or JIT; execution and codegen live entirely in fusevm,
the shared engine behind zshrs, stryke, awkrs, elisp, ruby, arb, and pythonrs. A
tracing Cranelift JIT compiles hot arithmetic loops.
.SH 4. TOOLING
.SS Language server (\-\-lsp)
.B php \-\-lsp
speaks LSP over stdio: completion and hover from the symbol corpus (the same table
that generates
.IR docs/reference.html ),
and diagnostics from the runtime's own parser. It is read\-only; no output reaches
the terminal.
.SS Debugger (\-\-dap)
.B php \-\-dap
speaks the Debug Adapter Protocol over stdio: line breakpoints, single\-stepping,
a stack trace, and inspection of a frame's locals. Program output is captured and
forwarded as
.B output
events so it never corrupts the protocol channel.
.SS Inline-Rust FFI
A
.B rust { pub extern "C" fn \[u2026] }
block desugars to an internal
.BR __rust_compile ,
compiles to a cached
.B cdylib
on first run (via the shared
.B fusevm
FFI runtime), and its exports become callable by name from PHP
.RB ( src/rust_ffi.rs ).
.SS Dumps
.B \-\-dump\-tokens
prints the token stream,
.B \-\-dump\-ast
the parsed AST, and
.B \-\-disasm
a fusevm bytecode disassembly \(em each then exits.
.SH 5. DIAGNOSTICS
\fIWarning\fR and \fIDeprecated\fR notices go to standard OUTPUT, interleaved with
the program's own, as the PHP CLI defaults put them; a fatal or parse error is
displayed there too and logged to standard error with a \fIPHP \fR prefix. Each
notice carries an \fIE_*\fR level and appears only when that bit is set in the
\fIerror_reporting\fR mask, which
.BR error_reporting (),
.BR ini_set ()
and
.B \-d error_reporting=\fILEVEL\fR
write. Notices raised while READING the source, such as \fIUsing ${var} in
strings is deprecated\fR, precede all program output and answer only to
.BR \-d .
The process exits 255 on a parse or fatal error, 1 on a failure with no PHP
equivalent, and 0 on success.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR php (1)
The focused invocation page. Source and issue tracker:
https://github.com/MenkeTechnologies/phplang
.SH AUTHOR
Part of the fusevm language family.
